('bulk-discount','dbn.Eurostat.nrg_pc_205.S.6000.MWH_GE150000.KWH.X_TAX.EUR.NL','NLD','Electricity prices for the selected non-household consumption band.','Bands classify annual consumption, not factories versus data centres. Prices exclude taxes here. Country and band gaps also reflect contracts, load profiles and aggregation weights; they do not identify a causal bulk-purchase discount or relocation effect.'),
('bulk-discount','dbn.Eurostat.nrg_pc_205.S.6000.MWH_GE150000.KWH.X_TAX.EUR.PL','POL','Electricity prices for the selected non-household consumption band.','Bands classify annual consumption, not factories versus data centres. Prices exclude taxes here. Country and band gaps also reflect contracts, load profiles and aggregation weights; they do not identify a causal bulk-purchase discount or relocation effect.'),
('bulk-discount','dbn.Eurostat.nrg_pc_205.S.6000.MWH_GE150000.KWH.X_TAX.EUR.SE','SWE','Electricity prices for the selected non-household consumption band.','Bands classify annual consumption, not factories versus data centres. Prices exclude taxes here. Country and band gaps also reflect contracts, load profiles and aggregation weights; they do not identify a causal bulk-purchase discount or relocation effect.'),
('china-mirror','dbn.NBS.A_A0406.A040608','CHN','Employment in China''s covered IT and software urban units rose from 3.64 million in 2016 to 5.53 million in 2024.','The staged annual observations are 364.0667 and 553.4 in units of ten thousand persons. Scope is the covered urban-unit population, not all IT workers; ownership and survey-frame crosswalks remain to be checked.'),
('china-mirror','dbn.NBS.A_A040I.A040I08','CHN','Average annual pay in China''s covered IT and software urban units was ¥122,478 in 2016 and ¥238,966 in 2024.','These nominal endpoints are reproduced in staging. Without a compatible deflator and comparison sector, the increase does not establish real-wage growth or relative AI-sector performance.'),
('chip-prices','fred.PCU334413334413','USA','US semiconductor producer prices provide a hardware-price comparison.','This basket is narrower than all electronic equipment and is not GPU price per unit of useful AI work. Quality adjustment and changing products matter; a flat index does not establish a halt in technical progress.'),
('chip-prices','fred.PCU333242333242','USA','Producer or export prices of semiconductor-making equipment.','Read each series in its own currency, base and market scope. Equipment prices are not quantities ordered or capacity delivered, and do not mechanically lead capacity.'),
('chip-prices','dbn.BOJ.CGPI.2300440015','JPN','Producer or export prices of semiconductor-making equipment.','Read each series in its own currency, base and market scope. Equipment prices are not quantities ordered or capacity delivered, and do not mechanically lead capacity.'),
('chip-prices','fred.IPG334S','USA','The selected production or labour-productivity series supplies a broad comparison.','Check sector scope before relating it to a narrower price index or another agency''s growth-accounting contribution. These series are not automatically components of one matched decomposition.'),
('chip-prices','epoch.gpu_price_performance',NULL,'Reported GPU price-performance observations illustrate hardware change.','Precision, workload, list versus transaction prices and hardware generations must be matched before computing an improvement factor. This series is not a quality-adjusted AI service-price index.'),
('clerical','fred.LNU02032207','USA','Employment in the selected clerical or administrative classification.','Occupational definitions and survey breaks differ across sources and countries. Compare consistent within-series segments; stable employment does not rule out displacement relative to an unobserved counterfactual.'),
('clerical','dbn.ILO.EMP_TEMP_SEX_OCU_NB.USA.BA_453.OCU_ISCO08_4.SEX_T.A','USA','Employment in the selected clerical or administrative classification.','Occupational definitions and survey breaks differ across sources and countries. Compare consistent within-series segments; stable employment does not rule out displacement relative to an unobserved counterfactual.'),
('clerical','derived.information_employment_share','USA','Information-sector employment as a share of total US payroll employment.','This ratio describes relative employment, not a business-cycle-adjusted AI effect. Both numerator and denominator can change for unrelated reasons; use a common period when calculating peaks.'),
('clerical','dbn.ILO.EMP_TEMP_SEX_OCU_NB.BRA.BX_6355.OCU_ISCO08_4.SEX_T.A','BRA','Employment in the selected clerical or administrative classification.','Occupational definitions and survey breaks differ across sources and countries. Compare consistent within-series segments; stable employment does not rule out displacement relative to an unobserved counterfactual.'),
('clerical','dbn.ILO.EMP_TEMP_SEX_OCU_NB.DEU.BA_2242.OCU_ISCO08_4.SEX_T.A','DEU','Employment in the selected clerical or administrative classification.','Occupational definitions and survey breaks differ across sources and countries. Compare consistent within-series segments; stable employment does not rule out displacement relative to an unobserved counterfactual.'),
('clerical','dbn.ILO.EMP_TEMP_SEX_OCU_NB.FRA.BA_148.OCU_ISCO08_4.SEX_T.A','FRA','Employment in the selected clerical or administrative classification.','Occupational definitions and survey breaks differ across sources and countries. Compare consistent within-series segments; stable employment does not rule out displacement relative to an unobserved counterfactual.'),
('clerical','dbn.ILO.EMP_TEMP_SEX_OCU_NB.GBR.BA_2247.OCU_ISCO08_4.SEX_T.A','GBR','Employment in the selected clerical or administrative classification.','Occupational definitions and survey breaks differ across sources and countries. Compare consistent within-series segments; stable employment does not rule out displacement relative to an unobserved counterfactual.'),
('clerical','dbn.ILO.EMP_TEMP_SEX_OCU_NB.JPN.BA_259.OCU_ISCO08_4.SEX_T.A','JPN','Employment in the selected clerical or administrative classification.','Occupational definitions and survey breaks differ across sources and countries. Compare consistent within-series segments; stable employment does not rule out displacement relative to an unobserved counterfactual.'),
('clerical','dbn.ILO.EMP_TEMP_SEX_OCU_NB.KOR.BA_222.OCU_ISCO08_4.SEX_T.A','KOR','Employment in the selected clerical or administrative classification.','Occupational definitions and survey breaks differ across sources and countries. Compare consistent within-series segments; stable employment does not rule out displacement relative to an unobserved counterfactual.'),
('computer-dividend','dbn.OECD.DSD_PDB_DF_PDB_GR.USA.A.ICTHRS_PCCONLP._T.PD.V.GOY._Z._Z','USA','The growth-accounting contribution of ICT capital deepening to labour-productivity growth.','This is a percentage-point contribution, not a return on AI investment. ICT includes non-AI assets, and labour-productivity growth also reflects labour composition and multifactor productivity.'),
('computer-dividend','dbn.OECD.DSD_PDB_DF_PDB_GR.USA.A.SOFT_PCCONK._T.PD.V.GOY._Z._Z','USA','Software and databases'' contribution to measured capital growth.','Its denominator differs from a contribution to labour-productivity growth. Comparing the two does not measure investment returns or establish that expenditure is at a historical boom rate.'),
('computer-dividend','fred.B985RC1Q027SBEA','USA','US fixed investment in the selected information-processing asset category.','Investment is an expenditure flow, not a capital stock or capital deepening. Current-dollar values require matched prices for volume growth; spending totals do not reveal whether financing came from operations, debt or equity.'),
('computer-dividend','fred.OPHNFB','USA','The selected production or labour-productivity series supplies a broad comparison.','Check sector scope before relating it to a narrower price index or another agency''s growth-accounting contribution. These series are not automatically components of one matched decomposition.'),
('dot-com','fred.B985RC1Q027SBEA','USA','US fixed investment in software, within broader digital investment.','BEA capitalises qualifying software in national accounts, including internally produced software. Firm financial-accounting treatment is not uniform; nominal spending composition does not identify whether an AI boom is driven by code or chips.'),
('dot-com','wb.NE.GDI.FTOT.ZS','WLD','Gross fixed capital formation as a share of GDP provides an investment-intensity benchmark.','A flat aggregate ratio can coexist with a large sectoral change because other investment or GDP moves. Reporting-country counts do not prove that a published annual aggregate will be revised upward.'),
('entry-level','fred.LNS14024887','USA','Unemployment among younger workers provides an early-career labour-market indicator.','Age or educational attainment is not direct task exposure. A change cannot be attributed to AI without a comparison design; task productivity evidence does not establish hiring effects.'),
('entry-level','fred.LRHU24TTKRM156S','KOR','South Korean business AI adoption provides another national comparison.','Survey year, enterprise-size threshold and questionnaire must be matched before ranking countries; this is not a natural experiment.'),
('entry-level','fred.LRHU24TTGBM156S','GBR','Youth unemployment in the United Kingdom.','Use the displayed observation dates and current coverage rather than a fixed assumption about the release delay relative to the United States.'),
('entry-level','fred.LRHU24TTDEM156S','DEU','Youth unemployment in the selected European economy.','Institutions and macroeconomic conditions may matter, but this chart does not estimate their separate effects or identify an AI effect.'),
('entry-level','fred.LRHU24TTFRM156S','FRA','Youth unemployment in the selected European economy.','Institutions and macroeconomic conditions may matter, but this chart does not estimate their separate effects or identify an AI effect.'),
('entry-level','fred.LRHU24TTJPM156S','JPN','Japanese employment and unemployment provide a separate national labour-market comparison.','Demography, participation, demand and institutions can affect this series. Japan is not an untreated control for AI exposure.'),
('entry-level','fred.CGBD2534','USA','Unemployment among younger workers provides an early-career labour-market indicator.','Age or educational attainment is not direct task exposure. A change cannot be attributed to AI without a comparison design; task productivity evidence does not establish hiring effects.'),
('exposed-productivity','dbn.ONS.PRDY.DJR5.Q','GBR','Output per hour for the selected sector or economy.','Compare growth within consistent series. A common base does not equalise sector composition or methodology; extrapolating the pre-AI trend is one candidate benchmark, not an identified counterfactual.'),
('exposed-productivity','dbn.ONS.PRDY.GYY7.Q','GBR','Output per hour for the selected sector or economy.','Compare growth within consistent series. A common base does not equalise sector composition or methodology; extrapolating the pre-AI trend is one candidate benchmark, not an identified counterfactual.'),
('exposed-productivity','dbn.Eurostat.nama_10_lp_a21.A.I15.J.RLPR_HW.EU27_2020',NULL,'Output per hour for the selected sector or economy.','Compare growth within consistent series. A common base does not equalise sector composition or methodology; extrapolating the pre-AI trend is one candidate benchmark, not an identified counterfactual.'),
('exposed-productivity','dbn.Eurostat.isoc_eb_ain2.A.GE10.J62_J63.E_AI_TANY.PC_ENT.EU27_2020',NULL,'Reported AI adoption in European programming and IT consultancy businesses.','This narrower EU sector motivates a hypothesis about exposure. It is not direct evidence of AI adoption in every UK information-and-communication business or an explanation of its productivity growth.'),
('frontier-compute','epoch.training_compute_frontier',NULL,'Estimated floating-point operations in the largest documented model-training run.','This is computation performed over a run, not instantaneous electrical power or installed capacity. Hardware efficiency, duration, utilisation and reporting uncertainty affect the connection to electricity demand.'),
('frontier-compute','epoch.gpu_cluster_count','USA','Publicly documented GPU infrastructure provides a partial view of the build-out.','The register has uneven coverage and may include planned systems. Check operational status and dates before reading counts or MW as installed capacity; documentation timing is not necessarily construction timing.'),
('frontier-compute','derived.datacentre_capacity_mw','USA','Publicly documented GPU infrastructure provides a partial view of the build-out.','The register has uneven coverage and may include planned systems. Check operational status and dates before reading counts or MW as installed capacity; documentation timing is not necessarily construction timing.'),
('frontier-compute','fred.PCU518210518210','USA','US data-processing, hosting and related-service producer prices.','The industry basket is broader than AI compute and not directly comparable to compensation per hour or unit labour costs. BLS research documents quality-adjustment challenges; a price change alone does not identify compliance costs or substitution incentives.'),
('jobs','derived.information_employment_share','USA','Information-sector employment as a share of total US payroll employment.','This ratio describes relative employment, not a business-cycle-adjusted AI effect. Both numerator and denominator can change for unrelated reasons; use a common period when calculating peaks.'),
('jobs','fred.USINFO','USA','Employment in the US information industry.','The January–July 2026 staging mean is about 2.786 million. NAICS Information is broader than AI or software; its components need separate evidence rather than a claim that all have shed jobs since 2001.'),
('jobs','fred.PAYEMS','USA','Total US payroll employment supplies the denominator for sector employment shares.','It is a broad benchmark, not an untreated control group. Use matching months when computing ratios and distinguish partial-year means from annual observations.'),
('jobs','dbn.ILO.EMP_TEMP_SEX_OCU_NB.USA.BA_453.OCU_ISCO08_4.SEX_T.A','USA','Employment in the selected clerical or administrative classification.','Occupational definitions and survey breaks differ across sources and countries. Compare consistent within-series segments; stable employment does not rule out displacement relative to an unobserved counterfactual.'),
('jobs','dbn.Eurostat.isoc_sks_itspt.A.PC_EMP.EU27_2020',NULL,'ICT specialists as a share of employment in the European Union.','This stock includes occupations beyond AI. Its path does not identify hiring, displacement or the counterfactual number of specialists.'),
('jobs','dbn.STATJP.MIm.M.EP.B.TTP.SA','JPN','Japanese employment and unemployment provide a separate national labour-market comparison.','Demography, participation, demand and institutions can affect this series. Japan is not an untreated control for AI exposure.'),
('jobs','dbn.NBS.A_A0406.A040608','CHN','Employment in China''s covered IT and software urban units.','The survey population is not all workers in the economy. Check the source''s ownership, unit and classification coverage before comparing with another country''s payroll or household survey.'),
('jobs','wb.SL.UEM.TOTL.ZS','USA','Aggregate unemployment provides labour-market context.','Whole-economy unemployment combines technology, demand, participation and other influences. Its movement neither identifies nor rules out AI-related displacement.'),
('jobs','fred.LNU02032207','USA','Employment in the selected clerical or administrative classification.','Occupational definitions and survey breaks differ across sources and countries. Compare consistent within-series segments; stable employment does not rule out displacement relative to an unobserved counterfactual.'),
('markets','fred.PCU518210518210','USA','US data-processing, hosting and related-service producer prices.','The industry basket is broader than AI compute and not directly comparable to compensation per hour or unit labour costs. BLS research documents quality-adjustment challenges; a price change alone does not identify compliance costs or substitution incentives.'),
('markets','fred.PCU334413334413','USA','US semiconductor producer prices provide a hardware-price comparison.','This basket is narrower than all electronic equipment and is not GPU price per unit of useful AI work. Quality adjustment and changing products matter; a flat index does not establish a halt in technical progress.'),
('markets','fred.PCU333242333242','USA','Producer or export prices of semiconductor-making equipment.','Read each series in its own currency, base and market scope. Equipment prices are not quantities ordered or capacity delivered, and do not mechanically lead capacity.'),
('markets','dbn.BOJ.SPPI.5201330001','JPN','Japanese software or cloud-application service prices.','A common base supports comparing index changes, not price levels. Divergence between these baskets does not isolate the prices of people versus machines or demonstrate automation.'),
('markets','dbn.BOJ.SPPI.5201350004','JPN','Japanese software or cloud-application service prices.','A common base supports comparing index changes, not price levels. Divergence between these baskets does not isolate the prices of people versus machines or demonstrate automation.'),
('markets','dbn.BOJ.CGPI.2300440015','JPN','Producer or export prices of semiconductor-making equipment.','Read each series in its own currency, base and market scope. Equipment prices are not quantities ordered or capacity delivered, and do not mechanically lead capacity.'),
('markets','fred.PALLFNFINDEXM',NULL,'Broad market prices provide macroeconomic context.','Common movement does not distinguish an AI shock from other shocks. A whole-market index is not a causal test of regulation or a measure of AI-specific expected returns.'),
('markets','fred.SPASTT01USM661N','USA','Broad market prices provide macroeconomic context.','Common movement does not distinguish an AI shock from other shocks. A whole-market index is not a causal test of regulation or a measure of AI-specific expected returns.'),
('materials','fred.IQ12260','USA','US export prices for nonmonetary gold.','An export-price index is not the gold spot price or a direct measure of investor risk aversion; keep its base and market scope distinct from LBMA quotes.'),
('materials','fred.PALUMUSDM',NULL,'The selected metal price provides context for material costs.','Many industries demand these materials and supply shocks also move prices. This is not an AI demand estimate or a direct cost-of-compute series; check the displayed last observation rather than assuming another source is unavailable.'),
('materials','fred.PNICKUSDM',NULL,'The selected metal price provides context for material costs.','Many industries demand these materials and supply shocks also move prices. This is not an AI demand estimate or a direct cost-of-compute series; check the displayed last observation rather than assuming another source is unavailable.'),
('materials','lbma.gold',NULL,'The selected metal price provides context for material costs.','Many industries demand these materials and supply shocks also move prices. This is not an AI demand estimate or a direct cost-of-compute series; check the displayed last observation rather than assuming another source is unavailable.'),
('materials','lbma.silver',NULL,'The selected metal price provides context for material costs.','Many industries demand these materials and supply shocks also move prices. This is not an AI demand estimate or a direct cost-of-compute series; check the displayed last observation rather than assuming another source is unavailable.'),
('materials','dbn.IMF.PCPS.lithium',NULL,'The selected metal price provides context for material costs.','Many industries demand these materials and supply shocks also move prices. This is not an AI demand estimate or a direct cost-of-compute series; check the displayed last observation rather than assuming another source is unavailable.'),
('materials','dbn.IMF.PCPS.cobalt',NULL,'The selected metal price provides context for material costs.','Many industries demand these materials and supply shocks also move prices. This is not an AI demand estimate or a direct cost-of-compute series; check the displayed last observation rather than assuming another source is unavailable.'),
('materials','dbn.IMF.PCPS.uranium',NULL,'The selected metal price provides context for material costs.','Many industries demand these materials and supply shocks also move prices. This is not an AI demand estimate or a direct cost-of-compute series; check the displayed last observation rather than assuming another source is unavailable.'),
('money','fred.A679RC1Q027SBEA','USA','US fixed investment in the selected information-processing asset category.','Investment is an expenditure flow, not a capital stock or capital deepening. Current-dollar values require matched prices for volume growth; spending totals do not reveal whether financing came from operations, debt or equity.'),
('money','fred.B985RC1Q027SBEA','USA','US fixed investment in software, within broader digital investment.','BEA capitalises qualifying software in national accounts, including internally produced software. Firm financial-accounting treatment is not uniform; nominal spending composition does not identify whether an AI boom is driven by code or chips.'),
('money','dbn.BEA.NIPA-T50405.LA001282-A','USA','US private investment in data-centre structures.','Structures spending excludes equipment. The series has a short history and does not separate AI-specific uses; comparing its growth with all other accounts requires an explicit matched calculation.'),
('money','dbn.BEA.NIPA-T50505.B935RC-A','USA','US fixed investment in the selected information-processing asset category.','Investment is an expenditure flow, not a capital stock or capital deepening. Current-dollar values require matched prices for volume growth; spending totals do not reveal whether financing came from operations, debt or equity.'),
('money','dbn.WTO.ITS_CS_AX6.000.SI2.000.A',NULL,'World exports of computer services.','Exports exclude domestic sales and are not the whole world market. Nominal cross-border receipts complement but do not independently validate domestic real value added.'),
('money','fred.TLMFGCONS','USA','US manufacturing construction spending.','This includes non-AI manufacturing. Its movements alone do not separate industrial-policy effects, semiconductor investment and other demand.'),
('money','dbn.OECD.DSD_VC_DF_VC_INV.USA.VC_INV_MKT.LATER.USD_EXC.A','USA','US later-stage venture-capital investment.','This covers companies beyond AI and is a financing channel, not an AI investment total or a measure of how listed firms finance capital expenditure.'),
('money','dbn.Eurostat.nama_10_an6.A.CLV_I15.N117G.EU27_2020',NULL,'EU investment in intellectual property products.','This asset category is broader than software and databases. A sharp change can motivate investigation of composition or asset transfers, but does not identify relocation by itself.'),
('money','dbn.Eurostat.rd_e_berdfundr2.A.TOTAL.G-U_ICT.MIO_EUR.EU27_2020',NULL,'Business research expenditure in the selected digital-services category.','Check sector, funding scope, currency and price basis before comparing countries. Nominal expenditure growth is not real research-input growth or an estimate of AI research spending.'),
('money','dbn.OECD.DSD_ANBERD_DF_ANBERDi4.USA.A.MA.J62_63.USD_PPP.V.B','USA','Business research expenditure in the selected digital-services category.','Check sector, funding scope, currency and price basis before comparing countries. Nominal expenditure growth is not real research-input growth or an estimate of AI research spending.'),
('money','dbn.NBS.A_A0G11.A0G1101','CHN','Revenue in China''s software and IT services industry.','Annual nominal revenue in units of ten thousand yuan. The staged 2016 and2025 values imply approximately ¥4.823 trillion and ¥15.483 trillion; revenue is not real value added.'),
('money','wb.GB.XPD.RSDV.GD.ZS','USA','Whole-economy research expenditure as a share of GDP.','An intensity ratio is not the monetary denominator for a sector''s share of research expenditure. AI attribution requires a compatible breakdown.'),
('money','dbn.OECD.DSD_PDB_DF_PDB_GR.USA.A.SOFT_PCCONK._T.PD.V.GOY._Z._Z','USA','Software and databases'' contribution to measured capital growth.','Its denominator differs from a contribution to labour-productivity growth. Comparing the two does not measure investment returns or establish that expenditure is at a historical boom rate.'),
('money','wb.TX.VAL.TECH.MF.ZS','USA','High-technology goods as a share of manufactured exports.','This is a broad product classification, not an AI export measure. Compare the correct manufactured-export denominator rather than all exports.'),
('orders-and-output','fred.IPG334S','USA','Industrial production in the selected US industry or aggregate.','These are production indexes rather than output per hour. Matching base years makes index movements readable together but does not eliminate measurement differences or identify a technology effect.'),
('orders-and-output','fred.INDPRO','USA','Industrial production in the selected US industry or aggregate.','These are production indexes rather than output per hour. Matching base years makes index movements readable together but does not eliminate measurement differences or identify a technology effect.'),
('orders-and-output','fred.A34SNO','USA','New orders for US computers and electronic products, in current dollars.','New orders are a flow, not the backlog of orders awaiting delivery. Comparisons across years are nominal; a matched deflator is required for a volume comparison, and a narrower semiconductor PPI is not that deflator.'),
('orders-and-output','fred.PCU334413334413','USA','US semiconductor producer prices provide a hardware-price comparison.','This basket is narrower than all electronic equipment and is not GPU price per unit of useful AI work. Quality adjustment and changing products matter; a flat index does not establish a halt in technical progress.'),
('policy','derived.ai_regulation_volume','USA','AI-related Federal Register publication activity.','Search-derived counts depend on terms and retrieval completeness. They measure documents, not policy stringency, costs or current obligations; partial-year counts require a matching prior-year window.'),
('policy','derived.ai_binding_rules','USA','AI-related Federal Register documents classified as rules.','Publication is not the effective date. Rules can amend or withdraw requirements and differ greatly in scope; a document count does not measure obligations, compliance costs or the number of currently effective AI laws.'),
('policy','derived.ai_proposed_rules','USA','AI-related Federal Register proposed-rule documents.','Counts describe publications, not matched cohorts. Conversion rates and delays require linking proposals to subsequent actions, accounting for withdrawals and censoring.'),
('policy','derived.ai_presidential_documents','USA','AI-related Federal Register presidential documents.','The category is broader than executive orders. Legal effect, implementation dates and durability depend on the document; neither immediate effect nor relative speed is established by counts.'),
('power','dbn.Eurostat.nrg_pc_205.S.6000.MWH_GE150000.KWH.X_TAX.EUR.EU27_2020',NULL,'Electricity prices for the selected non-household consumption band.','Bands classify annual consumption, not factories versus data centres. Prices exclude taxes here. Country and band gaps also reflect contracts, load profiles and aggregation weights; they do not identify a causal bulk-purchase discount or relocation effect.'),
('power','fred.DCOILWTICO','USA','US WTI crude-oil spot prices.','A fuel-market backdrop, not a universal floor under electricity or compute costs. Energy substitution, regional generation mixes and contracts matter.'),
('power','fred.DHHNGSP','USA','US Henry Hub natural-gas prices provide one fuel-market comparison.','A US gas benchmark is not the European marginal electricity price or the fuel cost of every data centre. Local generation, network constraints and contracts affect exposure.'),
('power','wb.EG.USE.ELEC.KH.PC','WLD','The selected World Bank indicator provides a cross-country structural comparison.','Use the selected country''s dated annual observation and source definition. Fewer countries reporting the latest year do not by themselves prove that a published aggregate is a partial-year value or that its change should be discarded.'),
('productivity','fred.OPHNFB','USA','US nonfarm-business output per hour worked.','The staged annual mean rises from 103.63575 in 2019 to 117.9515 in 2025 (2017=100), about 13.8%. This is not flat, but it does not identify AI''s contribution. The J-curve is a conditional mechanism, not a guaranteed future payoff.'),
('productivity','fred.OPHMFG','USA','Manufacturing output per hour provides a sector comparison.','Sectoral and aggregate labour productivity can move differently because of input, output and composition changes. Sector effects need not appear before aggregate effects.'),
('productivity','fred.INDPRO','USA','Industrial production in the selected US industry or aggregate.','These are production indexes rather than output per hour. Matching base years makes index movements readable together but does not eliminate measurement differences or identify a technology effect.'),
('productivity','derived.productivity_gap_mfg_vs_total','USA','Manufacturing productivity relative to nonfarm-business productivity, rebased at their first common quarter.','Above 100 means faster cumulative growth since that base, not a higher productivity level. A ratio does not remove differential non-AI shocks.'),
('productivity','dbn.ONS.PRDY.GYY7.Q','GBR','UK market-sector output per hour.','Read the dated, numeric observations; missing values must remain gaps. A quantitative flatness claim requires a specified start, end and sensitivity to the period chosen.'),
('productivity','dbn.ONS.PRDY.DJR5.Q','GBR','Output per hour for the selected sector or economy.','Compare growth within consistent series. A common base does not equalise sector composition or methodology; extrapolating the pre-AI trend is one candidate benchmark, not an identified counterfactual.'),
('productivity','fred.RTFPNAUSA632NRUG','USA','Estimated total factor productivity provides a growth-accounting comparison.','TFP is a residual conditional on measured output, labour and capital inputs. It is not AI-specific. Its index base and vintage must follow the source metadata; measurement error and specification affect the residual.'),
('productivity','dbn.AMECO.ZVGDF.GBR.3.0.0.0.ZVGDF','GBR','UK total factor productivity from AMECO.','The release may combine historical estimates and forecasts. Use source-vintage status rather than a hard-coded calendar cutoff; values without verified status must not be presented as observed outcomes.'),
('productivity','dbn.RBA.H4.GNFPROSQI','AUS','The selected Australian productivity, labour-cost or vacancy measure.','Check the series'' units and source frequency. Missing future placeholders are not forecasts; label actual published forecasts only when supported by source-vintage metadata.'),
('productivity','dbn.RBA.H4.GNFULCYP','AUS','The selected Australian productivity, labour-cost or vacancy measure.','Check the series'' units and source frequency. Missing future placeholders are not forecasts; label actual published forecasts only when supported by source-vintage metadata.'),
('productivity','dbn.Eurostat.nama_10_lp_a21.A.I15.J.RLPR_HW.EU27_2020',NULL,'Output per hour for the selected sector or economy.','Compare growth within consistent series. A common base does not equalise sector composition or methodology; extrapolating the pre-AI trend is one candidate benchmark, not an identified counterfactual.'),
('productivity','dbn.OECD.DSD_PDB_DF_PDB_LV.USA.A.GDPHRS._T.USD_PPP_H.Q._Z._Z._Z','USA','GDP per hour worked in PPP-converted dollars.','PPP supports a qualified cross-country level comparison, not exact equivalence of sector coverage or methodology with the BLS nonfarm-business series.'),
('productivity','dbn.OECD.DSD_PDB_DF_PDB_GR.USA.A.ICTHRS_PCCONLP._T.PD.V.GOY._Z._Z','USA','The growth-accounting contribution of ICT capital deepening to labour-productivity growth.','This is a percentage-point contribution, not a return on AI investment. ICT includes non-AI assets, and labour-productivity growth also reflects labour composition and multifactor productivity.'),
('productivity','fred.RVASPI','USA','Real value added of US private services, including information.','This aggregate contains the information sector; it is not everything else in services or an independent control. Chained-dollar components are not generally additive outside the reference year.'),
('productivity','wb.NY.GDP.MKTP.KD.ZG','USA','Annual real GDP growth provides whole-economy context.','The series cannot isolate AI from other influences. It does not establish what growth would have been in a world without AI; use the selected country and dated annual observations.'),
('productivity','wb.NY.GDP.PCAP.KD','USA','Real GDP per person provides a broad living-standards-related output measure.','It is not household disposable income or a necessary short-run test of AI benefits. Demography, distribution and other shocks affect the relationship.'),
('productivity','derived.ai_news_volume',NULL,'The share of monitored news coverage matching an AI-economics query.','Normalising by coverage reduces sensitivity to total article counts, but changes in outlet mix, geography and query matching can still move the share. Attention is not economic activity.'),
('sector-output','fred.RVAI','USA','Real value added in the US information industry.','The industry includes publishing, audiovisual activities and telecommunications as well as computing services. Output and employment have different concepts and frequencies; a matched change does not identify an AI productivity effect.'),
('sector-output','fred.RVASPI','USA','Real value added of US private services, including information.','This aggregate contains the information sector; it is not everything else in services or an independent control. Chained-dollar components are not generally additive outside the reference year.'),
('sector-output','dbn.WTO.ITS_CS_AX6.000.SI2.000.A',NULL,'World exports of computer services.','Exports exclude domestic sales and are not the whole world market. Nominal cross-border receipts complement but do not independently validate domestic real value added.'),
('sector-output','dbn.WTO.ITS_CS_AX6.840.SI221.000.A','USA','US exports of cloud-computing and data-storage services.','Cross-border service receipts are not domestic compute sales or a quality-adjusted rental price. Rebased growth still requires consistent scope and dates.'),
('sector-output','wb.BX.GSR.CCIS.ZS','WLD','The selected World Bank indicator provides a cross-country structural comparison.','Use the selected country''s dated annual observation and source definition. Fewer countries reporting the latest year do not by themselves prove that a published aggregate is a partial-year value or that its change should be discarded.'),
('sector-output','wb.TX.VAL.ICTG.ZS.UN','WLD','The selected World Bank indicator provides a cross-country structural comparison.','Use the selected country''s dated annual observation and source definition. Fewer countries reporting the latest year do not by themselves prove that a published aggregate is a partial-year value or that its change should be discarded.'),
('total-factor-productivity','fred.RTFPNAUSA632NRUG','USA','Estimated total factor productivity provides a growth-accounting comparison.','TFP is a residual conditional on measured output, labour and capital inputs. It is not AI-specific. Its index base and vintage must follow the source metadata; measurement error and specification affect the residual.'),
('total-factor-productivity','dbn.AMECO.ZVGDF.GBR.3.0.0.0.ZVGDF','GBR','UK total factor productivity from AMECO.','The release may combine historical estimates and forecasts. Use source-vintage status rather than a hard-coded calendar cutoff; values without verified status must not be presented as observed outcomes.'),
('total-factor-productivity','fred.OPHNFB','USA','US nonfarm-business output per hour provides a labour-productivity comparison.','The gap with a separate TFP series is not simply capital deepening: labour composition, coverage and measurement methods can differ. Use a consistent growth-accounting framework for decomposition.'),
('total-factor-productivity','dbn.OECD.DSD_PDB_DF_PDB_LV.USA.A.GDPHRS._T.USD_PPP_H.Q._Z._Z._Z','USA','GDP per hour worked in PPP-converted dollars.','PPP supports a qualified cross-country level comparison, not exact equivalence of sector coverage or methodology with the BLS nonfarm-business series.'),
('vacancies','dbn.ONS.UNEM.JP9P.M','GBR','Job vacancies in UK information and communication.','Vacancies indicate reported labour demand, not completed hires or a guaranteed lead over employment. Read numeric observations with missing periods preserved.'),
('vacancies','dbn.Eurostat.jvs_q_nace2.Q.NSA.J.TOTAL.JVR.EU27_2020',NULL,'EU information-and-communication job vacancy rate.','A rate is not the same quantity as the UK vacancy count. Compare matching definitions, seasonal treatment and periods before drawing hiring-demand conclusions.'),
('vacancies','dbn.RBA.H5.GLFOSVTLF','AUS','The selected Australian productivity, labour-cost or vacancy measure.','Check the series'' units and source frequency. Missing future placeholders are not forecasts; label actual published forecasts only when supported by source-vintage metadata.'),
('vacancies','dbn.JILPT.e0208.M.1.1','JPN','Japanese registered job openings per registered applicant.','A ratio above one refers to the covered employment-service system, not all jobs and all people seeking work.'),
('vacancies','fred.ULCNFB','USA','US nonfarm-business unit labour costs and productivity provide a compensation-output comparison.','Unit labour cost equals hourly compensation divided by output per hour. It is not pay per hour or a price for a worker. Both productivity and unit labour costs can rise when hourly compensation grows faster; subtracting their index growth does not recover wages.'),
('ai-wages','fred.ULCNFB','USA','US nonfarm-business unit labour costs and productivity provide a compensation-output comparison.','Unit labour cost equals hourly compensation divided by output per hour. It is not pay per hour or a price for a worker. Both productivity and unit labour costs can rise when hourly compensation grows faster; subtracting their index growth does not recover wages.'),
('ai-wages','fred.OPHNFB','USA','US nonfarm-business unit labour costs and productivity provide a compensation-output comparison.','Unit labour cost equals hourly compensation divided by output per hour. It is not pay per hour or a price for a worker. Both productivity and unit labour costs can rise when hourly compensation grows faster; subtracting their index growth does not recover wages.'),
('ai-wages','dbn.NBS.A_A040I.A040I08','CHN','Average annual pay in China''s covered IT and software urban units was ¥122,478 in 2016 and ¥238,966 in 2024.','These nominal endpoints are reproduced in staging. Without a compatible deflator and comparison sector, the increase does not establish real-wage growth or relative AI-sector performance.'),
('ai-wages','dbn.RBA.H4.GNFULCYP','AUS','The selected Australian productivity, labour-cost or vacancy measure.','Check the series'' units and source frequency. Missing future placeholders are not forecasts; label actual published forecasts only when supported by source-vintage metadata.'),
('compute-price-abroad','fred.PCU518210518210','USA','US data-processing, hosting and related-service producer prices.','The industry basket is broader than AI compute and not directly comparable to compensation per hour or unit labour costs. BLS research documents quality-adjustment challenges; a price change alone does not identify compliance costs or substitution incentives.'),
('compute-price-abroad','dbn.BOJ.SPPI.5201450003','JPN','Japanese internet-data-centre service prices.','This is a service-price basket, not a constant-quality price for an AI computation. Read its own dated observations; a flat endpoint comparison does not mean prices never changed.'),
('compute-price-abroad','dbn.BOJ.SPPI.5201350004','JPN','Japanese software or cloud-application service prices.','A common base supports comparing index changes, not price levels. Divergence between these baskets does not isolate the prices of people versus machines or demonstrate automation.'),
('compute-price-abroad','dbn.BOJ.SPPI.5201330001','JPN','Japanese software or cloud-application service prices.','A common base supports comparing index changes, not price levels. Divergence between these baskets does not isolate the prices of people versus machines or demonstrate automation.'),
('cost-of-compliance','derived.ai_binding_rules','USA','AI-related Federal Register documents classified as rules.','Publication is not the effective date. Rules can amend or withdraw requirements and differ greatly in scope; a document count does not measure obligations, compliance costs or the number of currently effective AI laws.'),
('cost-of-compliance','fred.PCU518210518210','USA','US data-processing, hosting and related-service producer prices.','The industry basket is broader than AI compute and not directly comparable to compensation per hour or unit labour costs. BLS research documents quality-adjustment challenges; a price change alone does not identify compliance costs or substitution incentives.'),
('cost-of-compliance','derived.ai_regulation_volume','USA','AI-related Federal Register publication activity.','Search-derived counts depend on terms and retrieval completeness. They measure documents, not policy stringency, costs or current obligations; partial-year counts require a matching prior-year window.'),
('cost-of-compliance','fred.SPASTT01USM661N','USA','Broad market prices provide macroeconomic context.','Common movement does not distinguish an AI shock from other shocks. A whole-market index is not a causal test of regulation or a measure of AI-specific expected returns.'),
('diffusion-speed','wb.IT.NET.USER.ZS','WLD','Internet use provides historical context for technology diffusion.','The population is individuals, unlike enterprise AI surveys. Similar-looking adoption curves do not establish a matched diffusion-speed comparison.'),
('diffusion-speed','dbn.OECD.DSD_ICT_B_DF_BUSINESSES.OECD.A.G14_B.PT_ENT._T.S_GE10',NULL,'Reported AI use among OECD enterprises with ten or more employees.','The earlier draft''s displayed 5.6% and 20.3% imply 14.7 percentage points, not 14.5. Verify matching samples and years before treating this difference as a harmonised diffusion-speed estimate.'),
('diffusion-speed','dbn.OECD.DSD_ICT_B_DF_BUSINESSES.OECD.A.G14_B.PT_ENT.J.S_GE10',NULL,'Reported AI use among information and communication businesses.','NACE J includes more than software and telecoms. Sector composition and survey coverage matter; sector adoption levels do not establish an adoption ceiling or speed for other industries.'),
('diffusion-speed','dbn.OECD.DSD_ICT_B_DF_BUSINESSES.EU27.A.G14_B.PT_ENT._T.S_GE10',NULL,'Reported business AI use in the selected OECD or EU aggregate.','The enterprise population and survey frame must be matched by year. Neither aggregate covers every business in the developed world; mirror differences require checking release dates rather than assuming one source is permanently preferred.'),
('diffusion-speed','dbn.Eurostat.isoc_eb_ain2.manufacturing',NULL,'Reported AI use in European manufacturing businesses.','Compare within the survey population and reference year. A lower share than information services does not identify a number of years of diffusion delay.'),
('diffusion-speed','dbn.Eurostat.isoc_cicce_use.A.GE10.C10-S951_X_K.E_CC1_PANY.PC_ENT.EU27_202',NULL,'Businesses purchasing cloud services: a complementary digital-infrastructure indicator.','Purchased cloud services and AI use are separate survey measures. AI may be used through other arrangements; this share is neither a necessary ceiling on AI adoption nor an identified driver of diffusion.'),
('executive-action','derived.ai_presidential_documents','USA','AI-related Federal Register presidential documents.','The category is broader than executive orders. Legal effect, implementation dates and durability depend on the document; neither immediate effect nor relative speed is established by counts.'),
('executive-action','derived.ai_binding_rules','USA','AI-related Federal Register documents classified as rules.','Publication is not the effective date. Rules can amend or withdraw requirements and differ greatly in scope; a document count does not measure obligations, compliance costs or the number of currently effective AI laws.'),
('executive-action','derived.ai_proposed_rules','USA','AI-related Federal Register proposed-rule documents.','Counts describe publications, not matched cohorts. Conversion rates and delays require linking proposals to subsequent actions, accounting for withdrawals and censoring.'),
('expectations','fred.SPASTT01USM661N','USA','Broad market prices provide macroeconomic context.','Common movement does not distinguish an AI shock from other shocks. A whole-market index is not a causal test of regulation or a measure of AI-specific expected returns.'),
('expectations','derived.sec_ai_mention_rate','USA','AI mentions in sampled US corporate annual reports.','Mentions measure disclosure and attention, not verified deployment. Changing filing coverage, search terms and the denominator can alter the share; legal liability does not turn a mention into proof of operational use.'),
('expectations','dbn.OECD.DSD_VC_DF_VC_INV.USA.VC_INV_MKT.LATER.USD_EXC.A','USA','US later-stage venture-capital investment.','This covers companies beyond AI and is a financing channel, not an AI investment total or a measure of how listed firms finance capital expenditure.'),
('expectations','fred.PCU518210518210','USA','US data-processing, hosting and related-service producer prices.','The industry basket is broader than AI compute and not directly comparable to compensation per hour or unit labour costs. BLS research documents quality-adjustment challenges; a price change alone does not identify compliance costs or substitution incentives.'),
('is-europe-in-this','dbn.Eurostat.nama_10_an6.A.CLV_I15.N117G.EU27_2020',NULL,'EU investment in intellectual property products.','This asset category is broader than software and databases. A sharp change can motivate investigation of composition or asset transfers, but does not identify relocation by itself.'),
('is-europe-in-this','dbn.Eurostat.rd_e_berdfundr2.A.TOTAL.G-U_ICT.MIO_EUR.EU27_2020',NULL,'Business research expenditure in the selected digital-services category.','Check sector, funding scope, currency and price basis before comparing countries. Nominal expenditure growth is not real research-input growth or an estimate of AI research spending.'),
('is-europe-in-this','dbn.OECD.DSD_ANBERD_DF_ANBERDi4.USA.A.MA.J62_63.USD_PPP.V.B','USA','Business research expenditure in the selected digital-services category.','Check sector, funding scope, currency and price basis before comparing countries. Nominal expenditure growth is not real research-input growth or an estimate of AI research spending.'),
('labour-vs-compute','fred.ULCNFB','USA','US nonfarm-business unit labour costs and productivity provide a compensation-output comparison.','Unit labour cost equals hourly compensation divided by output per hour. It is not pay per hour or a price for a worker. Both productivity and unit labour costs can rise when hourly compensation grows faster; subtracting their index growth does not recover wages.'),
('labour-vs-compute','fred.OPHNFB','USA','US nonfarm-business unit labour costs and productivity provide a compensation-output comparison.','Unit labour cost equals hourly compensation divided by output per hour. It is not pay per hour or a price for a worker. Both productivity and unit labour costs can rise when hourly compensation grows faster; subtracting their index growth does not recover wages.'),
('labour-vs-compute','fred.PCU518210518210','USA','US data-processing, hosting and related-service producer prices.','The industry basket is broader than AI compute and not directly comparable to compensation per hour or unit labour costs. BLS research documents quality-adjustment challenges; a price change alone does not identify compliance costs or substitution incentives.'),
('labour-vs-compute','fred.PCU334413334413','USA','US semiconductor producer prices provide a hardware-price comparison.','This basket is narrower than all electronic equipment and is not GPU price per unit of useful AI work. Quality adjustment and changing products matter; a flat index does not establish a halt in technical progress.'),
('policy-lag','derived.ai_regulation_volume','USA','AI-related Federal Register publication activity.','Search-derived counts depend on terms and retrieval completeness. They measure documents, not policy stringency, costs or current obligations; partial-year counts require a matching prior-year window.'),
('policy-lag','derived.sec_ai_mention_rate','USA','AI mentions in sampled US corporate annual reports.','Mentions measure disclosure and attention, not verified deployment. Changing filing coverage, search terms and the denominator can alter the share; legal liability does not turn a mention into proof of operational use.'),
('policy-lag','fred.A679RC1Q027SBEA','USA','US fixed investment in the selected information-processing asset category.','Investment is an expenditure flow, not a capital stock or capital deepening. Current-dollar values require matched prices for volume growth; spending totals do not reveal whether financing came from operations, debt or equity.'),
('policy-lag','derived.ai_presidential_documents','USA','AI-related Federal Register presidential documents.','The category is broader than executive orders. Legal effect, implementation dates and durability depend on the document; neither immediate effect nor relative speed is established by counts.'),
('rule-conversion','derived.ai_proposed_rules','USA','AI-related Federal Register proposed-rule documents.','Counts describe publications, not matched cohorts. Conversion rates and delays require linking proposals to subsequent actions, accounting for withdrawals and censoring.'),
('rule-conversion','derived.ai_binding_rules','USA','AI-related Federal Register documents classified as rules.','Publication is not the effective date. Rules can amend or withdraw requirements and differ greatly in scope; a document count does not measure obligations, compliance costs or the number of currently effective AI laws.'),
('rule-conversion','derived.ai_regulation_volume','USA','AI-related Federal Register publication activity.','Search-derived counts depend on terms and retrieval completeness. They measure documents, not policy stringency, costs or current obligations; partial-year counts require a matching prior-year window.'),
('rules-vs-adoption','derived.ai_regulation_volume','USA','AI-related Federal Register publication activity.','Search-derived counts depend on terms and retrieval completeness. They measure documents, not policy stringency, costs or current obligations; partial-year counts require a matching prior-year window.'),
('rules-vs-adoption','dbn.OECD.DSD_ICT_B_DF_BUSINESSES.OECD.A.G14_B.PT_ENT._T.S_GE10',NULL,'Reported business AI use in the OECD survey population.','The earlier draft''s 8.7% and 14.3% are an increase of 5.6 percentage points, approximately 64%, not a doubling. This multinational sample is not a matched outcome for US regulation.'),
('rules-vs-adoption','dbn.OECD.DSD_ICT_B_DF_BUSINESSES.OECD.A.G14_B.PT_ENT.J.S_GE10',NULL,'Reported AI use among information and communication businesses.','NACE J includes more than software and telecoms. Sector composition and survey coverage matter; sector adoption levels do not establish an adoption ceiling or speed for other industries.'),
('rules-vs-adoption','derived.sec_ai_mention_rate','USA','AI mentions in sampled US corporate annual reports.','Mentions measure disclosure and attention, not verified deployment. Changing filing coverage, search terms and the denominator can alter the share; legal liability does not turn a mention into proof of operational use.'),
('sector-jobs','fred.USINFO','USA','Employment in the US information industry.','The January–July 2026 staging mean is about 2.786 million. NAICS Information is broader than AI or software; its components need separate evidence rather than a claim that all have shed jobs since 2001.'),
('sector-jobs','fred.RVAI','USA','Real value added in the US information industry.','The industry includes publishing, audiovisual activities and telecommunications as well as computing services. Output and employment have different concepts and frequencies; a matched change does not identify an AI productivity effect.'),
('sector-jobs','derived.information_employment_share','USA','Information-sector employment as a share of total US payroll employment.','This ratio describes relative employment, not a business-cycle-adjusted AI effect. Both numerator and denominator can change for unrelated reasons; use a common period when calculating peaks.'),
('sector-jobs','fred.PAYEMS','USA','Total US payroll employment supplies the denominator for sector employment shares.','It is a broad benchmark, not an untreated control group. Use matching months when computing ratios and distinguish partial-year means from annual observations.'),
('sector-jobs','dbn.BLS.ce.CES5051320001',NULL,'Employment in software publishing, separately from the wider information sector.','Industry-classification revisions and source-vintage coverage must be checked. An older mirror endpoint does not prove that no fresher official release exists.'),
('sector-jobs','dbn.BLS.jt.JTS510000000000000JOL',NULL,'Information-sector vacancies, hires or quits describe different labour-market margins.','Openings are a stock at the end of the month; hires and quits are flows during it. Timing and worker expectations are hypotheses, not effects identified by these series.'),
('sector-jobs','dbn.BLS.jt.JTS510000000000000HIL',NULL,'Information-sector vacancies, hires or quits describe different labour-market margins.','Openings are a stock at the end of the month; hires and quits are flows during it. Timing and worker expectations are hypotheses, not effects identified by these series.'),
('sector-jobs','dbn.BLS.jt.JTS510000000000000QUL',NULL,'Information-sector vacancies, hires or quits describe different labour-market margins.','Openings are a stock at the end of the month; hires and quits are flows during it. Timing and worker expectations are hypotheses, not effects identified by these series.'),
('skills-shortage','dbn.Eurostat.jvs_q_nace2.Q.NSA.J.TOTAL.JVR.EU27_2020',NULL,'EU information-and-communication job vacancy rate.','A rate is not the same quantity as the UK vacancy count. Compare matching definitions, seasonal treatment and periods before drawing hiring-demand conclusions.'),
('skills-shortage','dbn.Eurostat.isoc_ske_itrcrn2.A.GE10.C10-S951_X_K.E_ITSPVAC2.PC_ENT.EU27_2',NULL,'Enterprises reporting hard-to-fill ICT-specialist vacancies.','The PC_ENT denominator is enterprises in scope, not only enterprises that attempted recruitment. Check the reference period and denominator before comparing this share with vacancy rates.'),
('skills-shortage','dbn.Eurostat.isoc_sks_itspt.A.PC_EMP.EU27_2020',NULL,'ICT specialists as a share of employment in the European Union.','This stock includes occupations beyond AI. Its path does not identify hiring, displacement or the counterfactual number of specialists.'),
('skills-shortage','dbn.OECD.DSD_ICT_B_DF_BUSINESSES.OECD.A.H1_B.PT_ENT._T.S_GE10',NULL,'Businesses employing ICT specialists.','An organisational-capacity proxy, not a test of whether a firm can use AI. Outsourcing, existing software and job definitions also affect the measure.'),
('software-not-steel','fred.B985RC1Q027SBEA','USA','US nominal fixed investment in the selected digital asset.','Quarterly SAAR values are annualised rates, not expenditure summed within the quarter. Historical drawdowns and recovery dates require matched frequency and price treatment; asset categories have different scopes.'),
('software-not-steel','fred.A679RC1Q027SBEA','USA','US nominal fixed investment in the selected digital asset.','Quarterly SAAR values are annualised rates, not expenditure summed within the quarter. Historical drawdowns and recovery dates require matched frequency and price treatment; asset categories have different scopes.'),
('software-not-steel','dbn.BEA.NIPA-T50505.B935RC-A','USA','US nominal fixed investment in the selected digital asset.','Quarterly SAAR values are annualised rates, not expenditure summed within the quarter. Historical drawdowns and recovery dates require matched frequency and price treatment; asset categories have different scopes.'),
('software-not-steel','dbn.OECD.DSD_PDB_DF_PDB_GR.USA.A.SOFT_PCCONK._T.PD.V.GOY._Z._Z','USA','Software and databases'' contribution to measured capital growth.','Its denominator differs from a contribution to labour-productivity growth. Comparing the two does not measure investment returns or establish that expenditure is at a historical boom rate.'),
('software-not-steel','dbn.BEA.NIPA-T50605.Y003RC-A',NULL,'Investment in prepackaged, custom or own-account software.','National-accounts asset categories distinguish purchased and internally produced software. Own-account investment is valued rather than omitted; these categories do not map mechanically to firms'' financial-accounting expense treatment.'),
('software-not-steel','dbn.BEA.NIPA-T50605.Y004RC-A',NULL,'Investment in prepackaged, custom or own-account software.','National-accounts asset categories distinguish purchased and internally produced software. Own-account investment is valued rather than omitted; these categories do not map mechanically to firms'' financial-accounting expense treatment.'),
('software-not-steel','dbn.BEA.NIPA-T50605.Y005RC-A',NULL,'Investment in prepackaged, custom or own-account software.','National-accounts asset categories distinguish purchased and internally produced software. Own-account investment is valued rather than omitted; these categories do not map mechanically to firms'' financial-accounting expense treatment.'),
('the-buildings','dbn.BEA.NIPA-T50405.LA001282-A','USA','US private investment in data-centre structures.','Structures spending excludes equipment. The series has a short history and does not separate AI-specific uses; comparing its growth with all other accounts requires an explicit matched calculation.'),
('the-buildings','fred.TLMFGCONS','USA','US manufacturing construction spending.','This includes non-AI manufacturing. Its movements alone do not separate industrial-policy effects, semiconductor investment and other demand.'),
('the-buildings','derived.datacentre_capacity_mw','USA','Publicly documented GPU infrastructure provides a partial view of the build-out.','The register has uneven coverage and may include planned systems. Check operational status and dates before reading counts or MW as installed capacity; documentation timing is not necessarily construction timing.'),
('the-buildings','fred.A679RC1Q027SBEA','USA','US fixed investment in the selected information-processing asset category.','Investment is an expenditure flow, not a capital stock or capital deepening. Current-dollar values require matched prices for volume growth; spending totals do not reveal whether financing came from operations, debt or equity.'),
('when-noticed','derived.ai_regulation_volume','USA','AI-related Federal Register publication activity.','Search-derived counts depend on terms and retrieval completeness. They measure documents, not policy stringency, costs or current obligations; partial-year counts require a matching prior-year window.'),
('when-noticed','derived.ai_proposed_rules','USA','AI-related Federal Register publication activity.','Search-derived counts depend on terms and retrieval completeness. They measure documents, not policy stringency, costs or current obligations; partial-year counts require a matching prior-year window.'),
('when-noticed','derived.ai_binding_rules','USA','AI-related Federal Register documents classified as rules.','Publication is not the effective date. Rules can amend or withdraw requirements and differ greatly in scope; a document count does not measure obligations, compliance costs or the number of currently effective AI laws.'),
('when-noticed','derived.sec_ai_mention_rate','USA','AI mentions in sampled US corporate annual reports.','Mentions measure disclosure and attention, not verified deployment. Changing filing coverage, search terms and the denominator can alter the share; legal liability does not turn a mention into proof of operational use.'),
('who-funds-it','fred.A679RC1Q027SBEA','USA','US fixed investment in the selected information-processing asset category.','Investment is an expenditure flow, not a capital stock or capital deepening. Current-dollar values require matched prices for volume growth; spending totals do not reveal whether financing came from operations, debt or equity.'),
('who-funds-it','dbn.OECD.DSD_VC_DF_VC_INV.USA.VC_INV_MKT.LATER.USD_EXC.A','USA','US later-stage venture-capital investment.','This covers companies beyond AI and is a financing channel, not an AI investment total or a measure of how listed firms finance capital expenditure.'),
('who-funds-it','dbn.OECD.DSD_ANBERD_DF_ANBERDi4.USA.A.MA.J62_63.USD_PPP.V.B','USA','Business research expenditure in the selected digital-services category.','Check sector, funding scope, currency and price basis before comparing countries. Nominal expenditure growth is not real research-input growth or an estimate of AI research spending.'),
('who-funds-it','wb.GB.XPD.RSDV.GD.ZS','USA','Whole-economy research expenditure as a share of GDP.','An intensity ratio is not the monetary denominator for a sector''s share of research expenditure. AI attribution requires a compatible breakdown.'),
